    "body": "This option allows users to define the way they would like files to be deleted. It's one of those features you assume you'll never use but will regret not having when you need it.\r\n\r\nAn example would be:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nopts = {\r\n  options = {\r\n    delete_cmd = \"trash-put\"\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nFeedback on documentation and implementation details would be appreciated as always. I just wanna see this useful feature happen.\r\n\r\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2023-07-03T12:34:32Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for taking your time writing this.\r\nAt the moment I don't think this extra option is a good fit for \"usefulness vs. complexity/maintenance\" traid-off. Also having a way to customize deleting but not other actions seems a bit off, which only adds to the complexity/maintenance.\r\n\r\nAm I correct understanding that your main issue with current `vim.fn.delete()` approach is that it deletes entirely while you want to move into trash?\r\n\r\nI'll think about the best way to handle this, but my hopes are not high for this to end up implemented.",
