        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "It's one of those features you assume you'll never use but will regret not having when you need it. One slip up in an untracked file and you'll be fishing around in the vim undo history before it's lost to time\n\n> At the moment I don't think this extra option is a good fit for \"usefulness vs. complexity/maintenance\" traid-off\n\ncertainly. the alternate solution is to have a `delete_cmd` option which takes a shell command to run. I think I like it more actually\n\n> Also having a way to customize deleting but not other actions seems a bit off, which only adds to the complexity/maintenance.\n\nI definitely thought about it, but decided that there weren't any other actions many people were going to realistically customise and to keep this pr short \n",
