        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "@mrshmllow, I've opted to adding module-specific \"trash\" functionality behind a new `options.permanent_delete` option. If set to `false`, it will move deleted entries to 'mini.files/trash' directory of Neovim's standard `data` path ('~/.local/share/nvim' on Unix). Here is [full info](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/f3648ab6ce4a5a44f632f98d5b6181a0463a5efc/doc/mini-files.txt#L587-L591).\r\n\r\nMy main reason for not going with `delete_cmd` is mostly because it is virtually Unix-only; Windows users probably won't install any CLI apps. \r\n\r\nAlthough I did not accept these changes, thanks for your enthusiasm to get this type of feature added.",
